  "verbalization": "Esketamine is linked to Anxiety Disorder through a series of pharmacological pathways that involve neurotic disorders. The evidence suggests that Esketamine may exert its effects on anxiety through the treatment of neurotic disorders, which in turn are indicated to treat anxiety. This chain of indications implies a potential mechanism by which Esketamine could influence the pathophysiology of anxiety, possibly by modulating neurotransmitter systems or altering neural pathways associated with emotional regulation. The consistent presence of neurotic disorders as a common intermediary in the indications supports the idea that Esketamine may act on these conditions, which are themselves linked to anxiety. The overlapping pathways across the three paths highlight a shared role in the treatment of anxiety, suggesting a possible mechanism of action that is both pharmacologically and biologically relevant.",
